# Git workflow

Full policy: [docs/development/branching-strategy.md](../../docs/development/branching-strategy.md), [docs/development/commit-guidelines.md](../../docs/development/commit-guidelines.md).

## Branches

- Branch from up-to-date `main`.
- Use short-lived branches: `feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `chore/`, `test/`, `refactor/`, `ci/`, `security/`.
- Delete the branch after merge. Do not accumulate long-lived feature branches.
- Never force-push `main`. Do not skip git hooks unless a maintainer or the user explicitly requests it and documents why.

## Commits

- Conventional Commits as specified in [docs/development/commit-guidelines.md](../../docs/development/commit-guidelines.md).
- Do not commit secrets, `.env` files, or real SBOMs. Do not rewrite unrelated files.

## Pull requests

Required checks live in [docs/development/branching-strategy.md](../../docs/development/branching-strategy.md) and [docs/development/ci.md](../../docs/development/ci.md). Run the equivalent locally as well and report actual results when GitHub-hosted jobs have not run. Complete [docs/development/review-checklist.md](../../docs/development/review-checklist.md). Add an ADR when the change is an architecture decision.

Do not merge with skipped tests unless a tracked reason is documented. Do not describe the tree as production-ready merely because checks passed.
